  "commands": [
   {
    "card": {
     "title": "From ticks to a weight"
    }
   },
   {
    "draw": [
     "scale",
     "tk1",
     "tk0",
     "l1",
     "l0"
    ],
    "speak": "Last time, four years at q = 0.5 became 2 QALYs — but where does a weight like 0.5, or 0.7, actually come from?"
   },
   {
    "draw": [
     "eq5d"
    ],
    "speak": "It starts with a short questionnaire, and the most widely used one is the EQ-5D."
   },
   {
    "draw": [
     "rl1",
     "rl2",
     "rl3",
     "rl4",
     "rl5"
    ],
    "speak": "It asks about five dimensions of health: mobility, self-care, usual activities, pain or discomfort, and anxiety or depression."
   },
   {
    "draw": [
     "grid",
     "h1",
     "h2",
     "h3",
     "h4",
     "h5"
    ],
    "speak": "In the EQ-5D-5L version, each dimension has five levels, from no problems to extreme problems."
   },
   {
    "draw": [
     "t1",
     "t2",
     "t3",
     "t4",
     "t5"
    ],
    "speak": "Our patient on the new treatment ticks one box per row — say, slight problems walking, moderate pain, and none on the rest."
   },
   {
    "draw": [
     "code",
     "states"
    ],
    "speak": "The ticks become a five-digit code, here 2 1 1 3 1: one of 3,125 possible health states."
   },
   {
    "camera": {
     "center": {
      "ref": "code"
     },
     "zoom": 1.8
    }
   },
   {
    "camera": {
     "reset": true
    }
   },
   {
    "highlight": {
     "target": [
      "t1",
      "t4"
     ],
     "effect": "circle"
    },
    "speak": "The code alone is not a weight: nobody has yet said how bad moderate pain is compared with trouble walking."
   },
   {
    "draw": [
     "vs",
     "vs_sub"
    ],
    "speak": "That is the job of a value set: a scoring formula estimated from a survey of the general public."
   },
   {
    "highlight": {
     "target": [
      "vs_sub"
     ]
    },
    "speak": "Members of the public value a sample of states, usually with the time trade-off, and a statistical model fills in the rest."
   },
   {
    "draw": [
     "a1",
     "a2",
     "q07",
     "lq07"
    ],
    "speak": "Feed in 21131, and the value set returns a weight — here, for illustration, 0.7."
   },
   {
    "draw": [
     "worst",
     "lworst",
     "luk"
    ],
    "speak": "The scale runs below zero too: in the 1997 UK value set for the older three-level version, the worst state scored minus 0.594."
   },
   {
    "highlight": {
     "target": [
      "t1",
      "t2",
      "t3",
      "t4",
      "t5",
      "vs"
     ]
    },
    "speak": "So a weight joins two things: the patient describes the state, and the public says what it is worth."
   },
   {
    "quiz": {
     "question": "The same patient's EQ-5D answers are scored in two countries and get different weights. Why?",
     "choices": [
      "Different value sets",
      "Different questionnaires",
      "The patient changed"
     ],
     "correct": 1,
     "right": "Different value sets: each country's public values the same states differently.",
     "wrong": "The ticks are identical — what else goes into the weight?"
    }
   }
  ],
  "sources": [
